er skin flag (`Mob::charge > 10` is it), water / lava drag of the ghast, the knockback of the explosion on mobs. Tests: `mobs::tests::{a_ghast_charges_twenty_ticks_then_fires_and_never_falls, a_fireball_accelerates_bursts_on_what_it_meets_and_turns_when_punched}`, `the_nether_spawns_pig_zombies_only` is now `..._and_ghasts_only`; the fireball's numbers (burst at y 10.9 on the grass from 20 blocks up, 1.3 blocks short of the player, top speed 1.9) were checked in a Python model of the same steps. UNVERIFIED: that it compiles (`ai_ghast` / `Fireball::tick` use `physics::aabb_hits_solid`, `ray_box`, `JavaRandom::next_gaussian` as their signatures read), the `lib.rs` wiring, the feel of the ghast's drift and the spawn rate by eye. Run `cargo test --lib mobs` first.
